runs from Jun 9, 2020 to Oct 14, 2020.","setup":"The stock rose about 51% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 7 weeks, peaking at $200.00 and pulling back 13% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Aug 26, 2020 it closed at $213.62, its first close above the base high of $200.00. Volume that day was 6.2M shares, 5.20x the prior 10-day average of 1.2M. It held, never closing below the level three days running, reached a best close of $243.88, and the chart ends at $230.54.","lesson":"This is an example of a textbook breakout: a base, then a close above it on heavy volume, and it held. This is the pattern the rules are built around."}}